            <AttackStep attackFeasibilityLevel="Medium" completeAttackFeasibility="Knowledge:null, Opportunity:null, Expertise:null, Equipment:null, Time:null" description="CAN messages can be tampered with freely only in a man-in-the-middle setup because of the active error frames of the sending ECU. &#10;&#10;Because of the open nature of the CAN bus, the situation when an ECU is pushed off the bus and the attacker starts impersonating the victim, is considered spoofing with other attack steps." mps:id="gvQG$2ywWq" name="ASC.0413" refinedBy="and(ASC.0412, ASC.0402, ASC.0404, ASC.0405)" title="TS - Tamper with CAN messages via MITM attack (vehicle frame)">
