            <AttackStep attackFeasibilityLevel="Low" completeAttackFeasibility="Knowledge:null, Opportunity:null, Expertise:null, Equipment:null, Time:null" description="Assuming that the attacker can perform arbitrary bit-banging, it is only needed to identify a target CAN ID that is transmitted by the victim ECU and then generate at least one bit of bus error after the arbitration phase.&#10;The purpose of a bus-off error is incrementing the error counters of an ECU and push it to error-passive and evenentually to bus-off state." mps:id="5El8qyGr$6k" name="ASC.0414" refinedBy="and(ASC.0407, ASC.0416)" title="TS - Bus-off attack against the ToE ECU (vehicle frame)">
