            <AttackStep attackFeasibilityLevel="Low" completeAttackFeasibility="Knowledge:K2(2), Opportunity:W5(5), Expertise:Ex2(2), Equipment:Eq6(6), Time:T5(5)" description="This attack is an evolution of the previous one. The goal here is to &#10;constantly set the brake demand to 0, preventing the driver from issuing &#10;a legitimate brake request. The method is the same as above, but with the &#10;addition of spoofed wheel speed signal values to simulate the vehicle slowing &#10;down during a legitimate request, preventing the ECU from detecting the attack." mps:id="2e6hrLrk78G" name="ASC.0418" title="DPRES + WSS">
                <InstantiatedClass>
                    <ThreatClassRef mps:id="5DSlnyktD3W" target="mps/r:bba387ab-3691-413e-99bf-ee48f7411463(GenericCatalog)/1HkBurD3Udx"/>
