            <AttackStep attackFeasibilityLevel="High" completeAttackFeasibility="Knowledge:K0(0), Opportunity:W0(0), Expertise:Ex3(3), Equipment:Eq4(4), Time:T1(1)" description="The attacker obtains (purchases or builds) a device that can be used to connect to and communicate on an automotive ethernet communication line.&#10;To perform arbitrary attacks, a MITM device is considered as necessary.&#10;&#10;Automotive ethernet is quite similar to standard ethernet, the main difference relevant here is that automotive ethernet uses different connectors, &#10;only two nodes are ever on a cable (point-to-point topology) and master/slave and speed is often not autonegotiated.&#10;Like standard ethernet, automotive ethernet can also have VLANs (providing segmentation and priorities), CRC checksums.&#10;Automotive application-level protocols include SOME/IP (Scalable service-Oriented MiddlewarE over IP) for the support of service oriented transmission of data, &#10;TSN (Time-Sensitive Networking) for low-latency transmission of streaming data (e.g. camera picture) and&#10;DoIP (Diagnostics over IP) specified in ISO13400 that is used e.g. for fast flashing." mps:id="3RcQOIlth_A" name="ASC.0702" title="Obtain Automotive Ethernet MITM device for modifying or sending packets">
