            <AttackStep attackFeasibilityLevel="Low" completeAttackFeasibility="Knowledge:null, Opportunity:null, Expertise:null, Equipment:null, Time:null" description="The attacker accesses memory locations that contain the firmware or cryptographic materials.&#10;This can be done by exploiting the UPLOAD, SHORT_UPLOAD XCP commands.&#10;The additional effort of determining the correct address to read (or extract later) is reflected in the &quot;reverse engineering&quot; attack step." mps:id="gvQG$2yABx" name="ASC.1203" refinedBy="and(ASC.0406, ASC.1201, ASC.2002)" title="TS - Read sensitive memory via XCP">
